  "background": [
    {
      "text": "In the case of an APU failure or misbehavior, the APU may automatically shut down, without a cooling period, in order to avoid subsequent damage.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCOM",
          "code": "DSC-49-30",
          "page": "P 1/2",
          "pdf": 2584
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "An immediate emergency shutdown, without a cooling period, occurs when the APU FIRE pb on the overhead panel or the APU SHUT OFF sw on the external power panel is pressed.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCOM",
          "code": "DSC-49-30",
          "page": "P 2/2",
          "pdf": 2585
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Some shutdown conditions apply only on ground with the engines not running: ECB failure, N overspeed and no speed. An APU fire shuts the APU down automatically on ground only. The full list is in FCOM DSC-49-30.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCOM",
          "code": "DSC-49-30",
          "page": "P 1/2",
          "pdf": 2584
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The FAULT light on the APU MASTER SW pb comes on when the APU has failed, an automatic shutdown is in progress, or an emergency shutdown has occurred.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCOM",
          "code": "DSC-49-20",
          "page": "P 2/10",
          "pdf": 2575
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
